---
description: Rules for editing Obtion notes (project status, tasks, decisions, wiki) in this vault
globs: Obtion/**/*.md
alwaysApply: false
---

- Notes in `Obtion/` with `kit: project|task|decision|wiki|record` in frontmatter are Obtion notes.
- Use only these statuses:
  - project `active|paused|done|dropped`
  - task `todo|doing|blocked|done|dropped`
  - decision `open|decided|superseded`
  - wiki `draft|published|archived`
  - record `active|archived`
- Human fields: `owner`, `due` (YYYY-MM-DD), `priority`, `project: "[[Name]]"`, `decided`, `verified`, `parent: "[[Name]]"`.
- Project notes keep `## Principle`, `## To do`, `## Done`, `## Verification limits` in that order.
- Never invent owners, dates, completion or verification; leave unknown values empty.
- Never mark `done`/`verified` without evidence the user can open.
- Never overwrite, rename or delete notes; never edit `.obsidian/`.
- When changing a status, append `- YYYY-MM-DD · status a -> b · reason` to the body.
- Propose bulk changes (more than five notes) before applying them.
